PATTERN 2: The H/|Aut| = #tilings decomposition as odd=even+odd
  For each class: #tilings = black + blue, where black=even, blue=odd.
  The specific (bk,bl) split is determined by the geometric class structure.

  (H, |Aut|) -> #tilings -> blue -> black -> bk/bl
    (   1,1): #t=   1, bk=   0, bl= 1, bk/bl=0.0
    (   3,3): #t=   1, bk=   0, bl= 1, bk/bl=0.0
    (   5,1): #t=   5, bk=   2, bl= 3, bk/bl=0.667
    (   9,1): #t=   9, bk=   6, bl= 3, bk/bl=2.0
    (   9,1): #t=   9, bk=   8, bl= 1, bk/bl=8.0
    (   9,9): #t=   1, bk=   0, bl= 1, bk/bl=0.0
    (  11,1): #t=  11, bk=   8, bl= 3, bk/bl=2.667
    (  13,1): #t=  13, bk=  10, bl= 3, bk/bl=3.333
    (  15,3): #t=   5, bk=   4, bl= 1, bk/bl=4.0
    (  15,5): #t=   3, bk=   0, bl= 3, bk/bl=0.0
    (  17,1): #t=  17, bk=  12, bl= 5, bk/bl=2.4
